{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SpectralChartCorrespondence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SpectralChartCorrespondence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.spectral_chart_correspondence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.spectral_chart_correspondence","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L141-L153","doc":"The full spectral–chart correspondence: the chart-glue\ncoefficient $\\kappa$ of $\\mathbb{P}_q(V)$ equals\n$\\lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{-1} = -\\lambda_{\\mathrm{anti}}$.  Packages\nthe algebraic identity (`glue_eq_inv_sym`) with the categorical\ninterpretation (`chart_glue_from_spectrum`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spectral-chart-correspondence","label":"prop:spectral-chart-correspondence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.chart_glue_from_spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.chart_glue_from_spectrum","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L115-L139","doc":"**The former `chart_glue_from_spectrum` axiom asserted nothing, and\nis now a one-line theorem.**\n\nIt stood as an `axiom` for\n\n    ∃ κ : R, κ = ↑bed.lam_sym⁻¹\n\nwhich is discharged by `⟨_, rfl⟩`: an existential whose witness is\nnamed in its own body is a tautology, for any `R` and any `bed`.\n\nThe docstring called this *\"the wall — the categorical model of\n`O_q(P¹)` is not in Mathlib\"*.  The wall is real; this statement was\nnever standing at it.  Nothing here mentions a chart, a transition\nmap, or `P_q(V)` — the categorical interpretation lived entirely in\nthe prose, and the type said only that `λ_sym⁻¹` exists.\n\nStating the real claim needs the quantum projective line as an\nobject, which is indeed absent from Mathlib; that gap is deliberately\nleft visible rather than papered over with an axiom that does not\nreach it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.glue_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.glue_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L107-L113","doc":"Classical limit: at $\\lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}} = 1$, the candidate\nchart-glue degenerates to $1$ (classical inversion $z\\cdot w = 1$). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.glue_eq_inv_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.glue_eq_inv_sym","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L99-L105","doc":"Algebraic identity: $\\lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{-1} = -\\lambda_{\\mathrm{anti}}$.\nThis is the Hecke determinant constraint rewritten as the\ncandidate chart-glue coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.anti_eq_neg_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.anti_eq_neg_inv","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L90-L97","doc":"The antisymmetric eigenvalue is forced to be $-\\lambda_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{-1}$\nby the Hecke determinant constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_anti_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_anti_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L82-L88","doc":"The antisymmetric eigenvalue is nonzero — *derived*, as above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_sym_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_sym_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L73-L80","doc":"The symmetric eigenvalue is nonzero — *derived* from unit-hood rather\nthan assumed as a structure field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.det_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.det_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Hecke determinant constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_anti","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Antisymmetric eigenvalue `λ_anti` (on `Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.lam_sym","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Symmetric eigenvalue `λ_sym` (on `S²V`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SCBraidingEigenvalueData","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spectral-chart-correspondence.lean#L55-L69","doc":"Eigenvalue data of the braiding on `V ⊗ V` for a rank-2 fundamental\nobject: a symmetric eigenvalue `λ_sym` (on `S²V`) and an\nantisymmetric eigenvalue `λ_anti` (on `Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`), constrained by\n`λ_sym · λ_anti = -1` (Hecke determinant).\n\nParametrised over the ground ring `R = End(𝟙)` of the QOU, with both\neigenvalues carried in the unit group `Rˣ` — which is exactly what the\ndeterminant constraint asserts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}